@@ -72,6 +72,25 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` adds a persistent listener like `on`, including the
+same argument forwarding and optional context. It returns an `unsubscribe`
+function for that specific registration:
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe(); // Removes only this registration.
+unsubscribe(); // Safe to call again.
+```
+
+Unlike `off` (or `removeListener`), which removes all matching listeners,
+`unsubscribe` cannot remove another registration that uses the same function
+and context. Cancellation is synchronous; listeners already captured by an
+emit continue to run, while later emits no longer invoke the cancelled
+subscription.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
